course: dictionary
lesson: 16052
title: Proved right at last
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Vindicated is a word for when people doubted you, laughed at you or blamed you, and then you were proved right. Think of it as "I was right all along." Look for clue words near it, such as doubted, blamed, proved or cleared.
explain: «Everyone laughed at Mia's idea, but when the experiment worked, she felt vindicated.» The clue is laughed at. Mia was doubted, and now she has been proved right, so vindicated means shown to be right.
explain: Vindicated can also describe how someone feels. «After three weeks, the judge found the man innocent, and he was vindicated.» Here it means cleared of blame, so everyone now knows he did nothing wrong.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in "proved right" and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Vindicated is the past form of the verb vindicate, which means to show that someone was right or innocent.
fact: «Vindicated» means shown to be right after other people doubted or blamed you.
fact: «Vindicated» can also mean cleared of blame, so people now know you did nothing wrong.
fact: As an adjective, «vindicated» means feeling happy and proud because you have been proved right.
fact: Common phrases are «be vindicated by», «feel vindicated» and «fully vindicated».
exercise: «The team said Kai's plan would fail, but it worked. Kai felt vindicated.» What does vindicated mean here? | Angry with the team | Very tired and sleepy | *Shown to be right after people doubted you | Lost and confused
exercise: «After the trial, Ruby was fully vindicated.» Which phrase means the same as vindicated? | *Cleared of blame | Given a new bike | Sent to bed early | Made to say sorry
exercise: «Feeling vindicated, Omar grinned at the people who had doubted him.» How does Omar probably feel? | *Happy and proud, because he was proved right | Hungry for lunch | Scared of the dark | Bored and sleepy
test: «Everyone said the robot would never climb the stairs, but it did. The inventor felt vindicated.» Why did the inventor feel vindicated? | *Because people had doubted her, and she was proved right | Because the robot broke down on the stairs | Because she forgot her plan | Because she won a prize for her lunch
test: «I told you the bridge was safe. Now the engineers have proved it, so I am vindicated!» Which words mean the same as vindicated here? | *I was right all along | I need a rest | I am lost and confused | I was wrong all along
exam: «The court said the journalist had told the truth, so her name was vindicated.» What does vindicated mean in this sentence? | *Shown to be right and cleared of blame | Written in a newspaper for the first time | Forgotten by everyone | Given a medal for running
